+/**
+ * PLAN_ORDER is not every federal plan. ED still offers PAYE and ICR on loans
+ * paid out before July 1, 2026, until both end by July 1, 2028 (34 CFR
+ * 685.209(c)(4) and (c)(5); for ICR, also 91 FR 34815), and ICR payments
+ * count for PSLF until then (34 CFR 685.219(b)(28)(iv)).
+ * Neither is priced here. Shown when payeAndIcrMayBeOpen() is true.
+ */
+export const SUNSETTING_PLANS_NOTE =
+  "PAYE and ICR are not shown here. If all your loans were paid out before July 1, 2026, you may still be able to choose them until they end by July 1, 2028. Where PAYE is open to you, it charges 10% of your income above 150% of the poverty line, never more than the 10-year Standard payment, and forgives what is left after 20 years. ICR can cost less for some borrowers going for Public Service Loan Forgiveness. Check both on studentaid.gov before you choose.";
+
 export const POST_CUTOFF_WARNING =
   "At least one of your loans was disbursed on or after July 1, 2026. That closes Standard, Graduated, Extended and IBR across your whole portfolio, including the loans you took out earlier. RAP and Tiered Standard are your only two options.";
 
